After breakfast, I take Tommy for a walk.
Outside, a light rain is falling.
I put the leash on Tommy's neck.
Near the busy road, he must not run.
He must always walk on the leash.
Suddenly, a stray cat comes in front of us.
He quickly pulls the leash to catch it.
I pull him back.
"Tommy, stop!" I tell him.
"You must not chase it."
"Stand there, wait."
He sits there and calms down.
We quickly return to the flat.
Tommy lies comfortably on his bed.
He is a good boy.
I take my umbrella and go to the café.
